.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M006.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"2600af9e","parentId":"2c03f255","timestamp":"2026-05-12T01:51:54.935Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the full picture. The repository currently has:\n\n1. `heretek-swarm/` - a nested subdirectory containing:\n   - `heretek_swarm/` - the actual Python package source\n   - `tests/` - tests\n   - `docs/`, `agent_workspace/`, `.claude/`\n   - `Dockerfile`, `pyproject.toml`, etc.\n\n2. `src/` - separate source directory\n3. `swarm-dashboard/` - frontend (already flat)\n4. `docs/`, `agent_workspace/`, `audit/`, `migrations/`, `tests/`\n5. Root-level configs (`.github/workflows/`, `docker-compose.yml`, etc.)\n\nThe issue is: the Python package `heretek_swarm` lives inside a directory also named `heretek-swarm`, creating a confusing nested structure:\n```\nrepo-root/\n  heretek-swarm/          # \"project\" directory (but confusing name)\n    heretek_swarm/        # actual Python package\n    tests/\n    pyproject.toml\n    Dockerfile\n  src/                    # separate source dir\n  swarm-dashboard/        # frontend\n  docs/                   # docs (root level)\n  ...\n```\n\nThe plan is to rename `heretek-swarm/` → `backend/` which makes it clear:\n```\nrepo-root/\n  backend/                # backend Python project\n    heretek_swarm/        # Python package\n    tests/\n    pyproject.toml\n    Dockerfile\n  src/                    # what is this?\n  swarm-dashboard/        # frontend\n  ...\n```\n\nNow I need to investigate the gray areas:\n\n1. What is `src/` at repo root? Does it duplicate `heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/`?\n2. What's the relationship between `src/` and `heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/`?\n3. What about the root-level `tests/` directory?\n4. Are there any other confusing overlaps?\n5. The nested `.actor_states`, `.benchmarks`, `agent_workspace` in the inner `heretek-swarm/` directory vs root level ones\n\nLet me investigate these gray areas further.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me investigate the gray areas in the repo structure - the `src/` directory and overlaps."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mwso68kk","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/src/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_nww44x2z","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0jhfg1dy","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/tests/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; ls -la C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/tests/ 2>/dev/null"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0ctb7mbj","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/heretek_swarm/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":159002,"output":754,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":159756,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778550699680}}
.gsd.migrating/activity/001-discuss-milestone-M006.jsonl:{"type":"message","id":"d3a3756f","parentId":"36a18ce9","timestamp":"2026-05-12T01:52:13.140Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me summarize the key gray areas:\n\n1. **`src/` at repo root**: Contains `__init__.py`, `cli.py`, and `agent_workspace/`. It appears to be a separate entry point package. Does this go into `backend/` too, or stay at root? The tasks mention `src/cli.py` as a file to touch.\n\n2. **Root-level `tests/`**: Contains ~50 test files. But there are also tests in `heretek-swarm/tests/`. The root-level tests look like the main test suite. The inner tests might be integration tests.\n\n3. **Duplicate directories**: `agent_workspace/` exists both at root AND inside `heretek-swarm/`. `.actor_states/` and `.benchmarks/` exist both in root AND inside `heretek-swarm/`.\n\n4. **`docs/`**: Exists at root AND inside `heretek-swarm/`.\n\n5. **`.claude/` exists inside `heretek-swarm/` but not root**.\n\n6. **Root-level `migrations/` vs nothing in inner**.\n\n7. **`swarm-dashboard/`** is correctly flat at root.\n\n8. The task T02 mentions `src/__init__.py` and `src/cli.py` as files for the import map - are they part of the restructuring?\n\nLet me also check: What does the inner `docs/` contain vs root `docs/`? And what about the `agent_workspace/` duplication?","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b95sde2q","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== ROOT agent_workspace ===\" && ls C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/agents/ && echo \"=== INNER agent_workspace ===\" && ls C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/agent_workspace/agents/ && echo \"=== ROOT docs ===\" && ls C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/docs/ && echo \"=== INNER docs ===\" && ls C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/heretek-swarm/docs/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4jb2n3bh","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== src/__init__.py ===\" && cat C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/src/__init__.py && echo \"=== src/cli.py first 20 lines ===\" && head -20 C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/src/cli.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6xtwaqbp","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:/Users/Derek/Desktop/heretek-swarm/.gsd/runtime/units/discuss-milestone-M006.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"LiteLLM","model":"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud","usage":{"input":163455,"output":649,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":164104,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778550715468}}
